      {
        "id": 234584,
        "name": "aramis",
        "username": "aramis",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/aramis/{size}/1871_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-01-14T06:07:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Having both...</p>\n<p>Both&nbsp;are are ratings in die sizes, both use dice tricks (count some, not all; reroll if...), both have provisions for creating bonuses and penalties...</p>\n<p>Cortex Plus/Prime. is one die from each of 3 to 7 categories (setting/adaptation dependent), keep two of choice, sum the kept for action total; unkept non-1 with most sides sets effect (Damage, temporary complication, possibly also scene boost assets)</p>\n<p>SC is always roll 3, 1 per category, for PCs and Villains, 1d for other NPCs</p>\n<p>There is common lineage - Cam Banks is in the preview pack.</p>\n<p>SC is kind of half-sibling of both Apocalypse World and Cortext...</p>\n<p>Cortex results really boil down to fumble, fail. success w/no or d4 result, success with d6 result, success &amp; d8, success &amp; d10, success &amp; d12... some flavors add high roll (&gt;5 over opp) as granting a bonus. Most rolls are opposed pools.</p>\n<p>SC has 5 discrete result bands (≤0, 1-3, 4-7, 8-11, ≥12) . Most rolls are unopposed.</p>",
        "post_number": 6,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:10:42.967Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
        "reads": 5,
        "readers_count": 4,
        "score": 1.0,
